{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OhtsukiKappaDependence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.OhtsukiKappaDependence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DominationTowers","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicVolumeTranscendence"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.relation_would_lift_4_1_grade","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.relation_would_lift_4_1_grade","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/OhtsukiKappaDependence.lean#L135-L141","doc":"Contrapositive on real data: were a polynomial relation to hold among the\nleading parts, the combined tower would have to leave grade `0`. With only the\n`4₁` tower available this is a statement about one knot, not the three-knot\nrelation `qou-7jok` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ohtsuki_4_1_grade_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ohtsuki_4_1_grade_zero","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/OhtsukiKappaDependence.lean#L122-L133","doc":"**The 4₁ tower has grade `0`.** Its leading coefficient is `Vol(4₁) ≠ 0`, so\nby `grade_pos_iff_leading_vanishes` the grade cannot be positive — and grade `0`\nis exactly the \"no relation\" reading.\n\nThis is the machinery of `DominationTowers` running on real data: the head is\nread by the grade, the (dependent, arithmetic) tail is not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa2_4_1_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa2_4_1_pos","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/OhtsukiKappaDependence.lean#L115-L118","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa1_4_1_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa1_4_1_pos","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/OhtsukiKappaDependence.lean#L107-L113","doc":"Both tail coefficients are non-zero, so the dependence is not the trivial\none — `288x² − 121y` genuinely relates two non-degenerate quantities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa_tail_annihilated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa_tail_annihilated","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/OhtsukiKappaDependence.lean#L102-L105","doc":"The same statement as an annihilator: `288x² − 121y` kills `(κ₁, κ₂)`, so\nthe tail coefficients are **algebraically dependent over `ℚ`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa_4_1_relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa_4_1_relation","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/OhtsukiKappaDependence.lean#L92-L100","doc":"**`288·κ₁² = 121·κ₂`** — an exact rational relation among the 4₁ Ohtsuki\ntail coefficients. Verified symbolically against the witness closed forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa2_4_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa2_4_1","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/OhtsukiKappaDependence.lean#L89-L90","doc":"`κ₂(4₁) = 2π²/27 ≈ 0.731081807488100`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa1_4_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa1_4_1","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/OhtsukiKappaDependence.lean#L86-L87","doc":"`κ₁(4₁) = 11√3·π/108 ≈ 0.554216472404899`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa_relation_formal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.kappa_relation_formal","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/OhtsukiKappaDependence.lean#L76-L82","doc":"**The relation is formal.** For any `s` with `s² = 3` and any `p`, the pair\n`(11sp/108, 2p²/27)` satisfies a rational relation — nothing about `π` or `√3`\nbeyond `√3² = 3` is used. Stated denominator-cleared so it holds over any\ncommutative ring. ","signatureChunk":0}]}